listing:   qmp_cmds.py; addr2line
toolchain: QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18); GNU addr2line (GNU Binutils for Ubuntu) 2.42
command:   python3 -I qmp_cmds.py serial.txt 'holding the log lock' 'sleep 3;info registers;x /16xb $pc' qemu-system-x86_64 -machine pc -m 128M -nodefaults -vga std -display none -no-reboot -kernel k_hang.bin; addr2line -f -C -e k_hang.elf <RIP>
date:      2026-10-09T20:53:39Z
machine:   Linux x86_64 (cloud build container)
exit code: 0
note:      segment, descriptor-table, debug and floating-point register lines are left out
hardware:  untested on hardware; QEMU 8.2.2 with TCG (no KVM in the build container)
